I guess that would mean reassigning this to sig-cluster-lifecycle to triage it , and decide wether or not such a change to the Kubeadm defaults was valid.

> No, I’m suggesting disabling dns cache for all the cluster domain (eg cluster.local), not individual records under it.

I've brought this up with them before but they didn't though disabling the cache for was a good idea, but perhaps only for misses is the right solution.

this is the `Corefile` k8s installs by default to the internal coredns
```
  Corefile: |
    .:53 {
        errors
        health {
           lameduck 5s
        }
        ready
        kubernetes cluster.local in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa {
           pods insecure
           fallthrough in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa
           ttl 30
        }
        prometheus :9153
        forward . /etc/resolv.conf {
           max_concurrent 1000
        }
        cache 30
        loop
        reload
        loadbalance
    }
```

so we would disable misses like this

```
  Corefile: |
    .:53 {
        errors
        health {
           lameduck 5s
        }
        ready
        kubernetes cluster.local in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa {
           pods insecure
           fallthrough in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa
           ttl 30
           cache {
                    disable denial cluster.local in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa
           }

        }
        prometheus :9153
        forward . /etc/resolv.conf {
           max_concurrent 1000
        }
        cache 30
        loop
        reload
        loadbalance
    }
```

is this a good assumption @chrisohaver ?

